   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the civil service law, in relation to requiring the president\nof the civil service commission to prepare and deliver a triennial report\nrelating to current programs within each state agency that allow for\nalternative work schedules or flexible work hours",
    "basePrintNo": "S7296",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7296-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §7, Civ Serv L (as proposed in S. 5811-A and A. 7634-A)",
    "lawSection": "Civil Service Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7296\n\nSPONSOR: KAVANAGH\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the civil service law, in relation to\nrequiring the president of the civil service commission to prepare and\ndeliver a triennial report relating to current programs within each\nstate agency that allow for alternative work schedules or flexible work\nhours\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nChapter 439 of 2017 required require the President of the Civil Service\nCommission to prepare an annual report determining the feasibility of\nstate agencies permitting alternative work schedules and flexible work\nhours.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one amends section 7 of the civil service law by adding a new\nsubdivision 7.\n\nSection two is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nAs amended, Chapter 439 will require the civil service commission to\nprepare and deliver a triennial report relating to current programs\nwithin each state agency that allow for alternative work schedules or\nflexible work hours beginning in September 2018.\n\nChapter 439 was further amended to add specific language protecting\ncollective bargaining agreements from being impacted by unilateral exec-\nutive rule making. Any recommendations or findings set forth in the\ntriennial report cannot \"impede, infringe or diminish the rights and\nbenefits that accrue to employees and employers through collective\nbargaining agreements, or otherwise diminish the integrity of the\ncollective bargaining relationship.\"\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as\nChapter 439 of the laws of 2017.\n",
